course: dictionary
lesson: 9327
title: Spider: a word with a clear meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word's meaning often shows in the sentence around it. «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» The clues tell you what a spider is: eight legs, two body parts, and no wings.
explain: Spiders and insects can look alike, so count the legs. Insects have six legs and three body parts. Spiders have eight legs and two body parts. When two things look alike, look for the number of legs and body parts.
explain: The word can also mean a thread. «Some spider silk is stronger than steel and very stretchy.» Here silk is the thread a spider spins, and the sentence tells you it is very strong.
fact: A spider is a small animal with eight legs that spins webs of silk to catch insects.
fact: Spiders are not insects. They belong to a group called arachnids.
fact: Most spiders are harmless to people, but a few have a dangerous bite.
fact: «Arachnids» are animals with eight legs and two body parts, like spiders.
fact: Spiders use webs to catch insects, so a web is like a trap made of silk.
exercise: «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no wings.» How many legs does a spider have? | Ten | Four | Six | *Eight
exercise: Which group does a spider belong to? | Birds | Mammals | Insects | *Arachnids
exercise: «Most spiders are harmless to people, but a few have a dangerous bite.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that means the opposite of harmless. | bite | most | *dangerous | people
test: How many body parts does a spider have? | Three | Four | *Two | Eight
test: What do spiders spin webs to catch? | Flowers | Stones | *Insects | Fish
exam: Why is a spider not an insect, according to «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings»? | Spiders are a kind of fish | *Insects have six legs and three body parts | Spiders have wings | Spiders have six legs
